//! The `offset` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property sets all the properties required for animating an element along a defined path. The
//! offset properties together help to define an _offset transform_, a
//! [transform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Transforms/Using) that aligns
//! a point in an element
//! ([offset-anchor](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/offset-anchor))
//! to an _offset position_
//! ([offset-position](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/offset-position))
//! on a path
//! ([offset-path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/offset-path))
//! at various points along the path
//! ([offset-distance](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/offset-distance))
//! and optionally rotates the element
//! ([offset-rotate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/offset-rotate))
//! to follow the direction of the path.
//!
//! Initial: offset-position: normal; offset-path: none; offset-distance: 0; offset-anchor: auto;
//! offset-rotate: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: offset-position: refer to the size of containing block; offset-distance: refer to
//! the total path length; offset-anchor: relative to the width and the height of the element's
//! reference box.
//!
//! Grammar: [ <'offset-position'>? [ <'offset-path'> [ <'offset-distance'> || <'offset-rotate'> ]?
//! ]? ]! [ / <'offset-anchor'> ]?
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/motion-1/#propdef-offset
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/offset
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

